              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Holiday Baker"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I so wanted to love this. One of my very favorite desserts is Boston cream pie. I liked that it had a slight creamy flavor, but it didn't taste at all like Boston cream pie in my opinion. I also thought it had a little bit of a strength to it, more likely from the amount of vodka. I ended up having to fix it, to cut through some of the vodka's strength. I didn't understand the point of the cherry either. Boston cream pie doesn't have cherries. If it was for decoration, it kind of just dropped to the bottom and dissapeared. I luckily though had some leftover in the fridge, from the holidays, so it wasn't an extra cost. I really wish this would have worked for me.",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-14T22:02:45.790Z"
